.TH HERCULES-STREAM100 1 "August 2026" "OpenStream100 0.17.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hercules-stream100 \- open the OpenStream100 control panel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hercules-stream100
.br
.B hercules-stream100 --migrate-user-install
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hercules-stream100
opens the OpenStream100 GTK control panel for assigning four physical encoders to active
PipeWire playback applications. The panel can start and stop the per-user mixer
service, choose channel colours, mixer backgrounds, and button-label overlays,
switch between the mixer, a separate full-screen image, and an editable notepad
with saved font size, family, style, text colour, and alignment,
adjust the hardware
screen brightness, and enable automatic startup at sign-in.
.PP
The controller is identified by USB ID 06f8:e053. The mixer drives its 480x272
display and supports per-channel volume, soft mute, saved Mono or Stereo audio
activity monitoring, four full-height native visualiser styles, and separate
percentage badges.
.SH MIGRATION
.B --migrate-user-install
moves an earlier installation from the user's local application directory into
a recoverable backup and switches systemd to the RPM-provided user service.
Saved assignments, colours, images, and button calibration are retained.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/hercules-stream100/config.json
Per-user channel assignments, colours, display mode, notepad text, brightness, images, and button calibration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/hercules-stream100/background.png
Application-managed copy of the selected display background.
.TP
.I ~/.config/hercules-stream100/fullscreen-image.png
Application-managed copy of the selected full-screen image.
.TP
.I ~/.config/hercules-stream100/button-overlay-custom.png
Application-managed copy of the selected custom 480x80 PNG button overlay.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/hercules-stream100.service
Packaged mixer service controlled by the application.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/hercules-stream100-display.service
Persistent display broker that retains the USB session across mixer restarts.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/openstream100/display.sock
Private per-user connection between the mixer and display broker.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR wpctl (1),
.BR pipewire (1)
